          <p>
            Read the motor figure with Landice’s own footnote. It calls the 4 HP a laboratory rating that shows
            how robust the motor is, and says household electrical supply limits the horsepower actually
            delivered. That honesty is unusual, and it means the 4 HP is not comparable with a home brand’s
            peak figure; our <a href="/treadmill-horsepower-guide/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">horsepower guide</a> explains the difference.
          </p>
