            touchscreen with 42 programs including virtual runs, HIIT and heart-rate control, user profiles,
            Strava and MapMyFitness syncing and entertainment apps, some of which need separate subscriptions.
            Every L7 has Landice’s control centre with speed and incline buttons, an emergency stop, a contact
            heart-rate bar, a safety lanyard, two bottle holders and a USB trickle-charge port.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>Orthopedic belt.</strong> A cushioned treadbelt that Landice says reduces impact on joints,
            for $325 on the L7. Landice’s promotion from 25 September to 5 November 2026 included it free, along
            with free shipping, delivery and installation; check whether a similar offer is running when you
            buy. Our <a href="/treadmill-cushioning-explained/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">cushioning guide</a> explains what deck and belt cushioning can do.
          </p>
          <p>
            <strong>The mount.</strong> Searches for "L7 treadmill Landice mount" are about the two accessories:
            a tablet mount for 7- to 12-inch tablets ($75) and a TV or monitor mount ($250), both sold as
            options on the L7 and as separate accessories. Landice also sells a $800 Landice Vision System. If
            you only want a tablet holder, our <a href="/best-treadmill-tablet-holders/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">tablet holder guide</a> covers cheaper options, though Landice’s fits its own console.
