            keypad and express speed and incline keys, nine built-in and five user programs, two HIIT programs,
            three fitness tests (Balke, Firefighter and Army), heart-rate programs and Bluetooth. Landice’s
            current store offers Pro Sports, Achieve and Elite instead, and we found no current listing using the
            code "L890CT". Given Landice’s code pattern (L890PST, L890AT), it is a reasonable reading of an
            L8 with a Cardio console, but we could not confirm it.
          </p>
          <p>
            In practice, an L890CT today is a used, remanufactured or dealer old-stock machine. The frame and
            drive are the same family as a new L8, so condition, the console’s state and whether any warranty
            transfers are what to check. Our <a href="/refurbished-treadmills/" class="text-[#0F62FE] font-medium">refurbished treadmill guide</a> covers what "remanufactured" should mean.
