        <div id="l7-rtm" class="scroll-mt-24">
          <h2>The Landice L7 RTM Rehabilitation Treadmill</h2>
<p>
            The L7 RTM (stock code L7-80 RTM) is the L7 adapted for physical therapy. Landice lists the same
            20 by 58-inch surface, motor rating, 15% incline and 400 lb capacity, and adds:
          </p>
          <ul>
            <li><strong>Extended medical handrails</strong> running the length of the deck, for patients who need support on both sides.</li>
            <li><strong>A very low starting speed.</strong> Landice’s text says "zero starting speed" and its spec list says 0.1 to 12 mph, while an icon on the same page says 0.5 mph. We cannot tell which is current; ask Landice or a dealer if a start below 0.5 mph matters for your patients.</li>
            <li><strong>A reverse option.</strong> Belt direction can be standard, or reversible with a remote stop/start, used in gait retraining.</li>
            <li><strong>Electrical isolation.</strong> A 300 micro-amp isolation leakage kit, a clinical safety requirement.</li>
            <li><strong>The Landice control centre</strong> rather than a programmed console, with an optional 19-inch HDTV monitor and mount.</li>
